From d546733bb63f1dc000e98db08a89ac63bc692fe2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 02:11:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/34] WP23: Filing watchdog

Every run of the deadline job (30 min) finds the stays that may miss their
police deadline: at least one reportable (non-Czech, EU included) guest not
accepted by UbyPort (submit_state != 'sent'), stay active and not archived,
property active, and deadlines.reporting_deadline from the earliest guest
arrival less than 24 hours away or passed.

- Host: one deadline_at_risk mail per stay (reservation.at_risk_mailed_at),
  with property, arrival, unfiled count, stay link and the manual UbyPort
  fallback. reminder_host is the check-in day nudge about guest forms, so a
  new kind.
- Operator: deadline_digest to UBYHOST_OPERATOR_EMAIL at most every 6 hours
  (settings key filing_watchdog_digest_sent_at), no guest names.
- UBYHOST_HEARTBEAT_FILING_URL: <url> when nothing is at risk, <url>/fail
  when something is or the deadline watch failed; no ping when the
  watchdog itself fails.
- Guide: "If UbyHost cannot file in time" (EN, CS).

Filed by hand: on the stay page the host can record "I filed this stay by
hand in UbyPort" with the filing time (default now) and an optional receipt
or reference. The stay's unfiled reportable guests become submit_state
'sent', so every existing filed-check and double-filing guard holds, with
guest.manual_filed_at, manual_reference, manual_marked_at and
manual_prev_state. collect_sendable never offers them (not even as a
resend), claim_sendable drops them, a guest under a live submission claim is
not marked. Status, the WP01 deadline badge ("Filed by hand 30.09. 14:32"),
the watchdog and the house book CSV and PDF treat and label them as filed by
hand. Audit stay_filed_manually; undo within 24 hours of the mark, audited
as stay_filed_manually_undone.

Unknown risk: a stay whose guests have arrived, with no guest entered, not
cancelled or ignored, and less than 24 hours to its deadline (or up to 7
days past it) gets the host mail once in a "no guest details yet" variant
and its own section in the operator digest. It never makes the heartbeat
/fail, because Czech guests owe no report.

Conflict resolution: db.py ADDED_COLUMNS, mail.py KINDS and HOST_KINDS, tests/test_claim_mail.py: kept PR 230's submission.retried_at column and cancelled_with_guests mail kind next to WP23's columns and kinds. guest_form_admin.html: WP23's filed-by-hand banner title with WP25's id="filed-lock-note". reporting.py: WP25 (earlier in this order) already defines _field(), so WP23's second copy is dropped. Carried in from earlier steps: tests/test_wp25_reported_bugs.py gets back its hand-filed variants (manual_filed_at), and the two hand-filing panels in reservation_detail.html use WP28's class="panel" (not panel tight), as WP28's padding fix requires.

PR 230 retry state: a guest on an outcome_unknown batch with retried_at still empty is waiting for the sweep's one automatic resend. filing_watchdog.at_risk_stays now joins the guest's submission; a stay whose every unfiled guest is in that state, before its deadline, is "awaiting the automatic resend" for at most RETRY_GRACE (two sweep intervals) from the batch's finish time: no host mail, no digest line, no heartbeat /fail. After the grace, after the resend (retried_at set), with any other unfiled guest, or once the deadline has passed, it is at risk as before. run() reports awaiting_retry; the scheduler logs it. New tests in tests/test_filing_watchdog.py; one existing stub takes the new keyword.

Owner change: no SMS. config.py, deploy/lightsail/.env.example and docs/plans/UbyHost_Audit_and_Cursor_Plan_2026-09-28.md now say the healthchecks.io filing check notifies the owner by e-mail (sent by healthchecks.io, so it arrives when UbyHost's own mail is broken). No code change.

Conflict resolution (WP31, earlier in this order): the sweep's one automatic resend has submission.mode 'auto_resend' and is never resent itself. The module docstring says so, and a new test checks that a stay held on an unclear resend is awaiting only within its grace and at risk after it, and still at risk five grace windows later. The watchdog code is unchanged.
